(1985890, 272792, 18207, '<td valign="top">Simplicity is great sometimes. Seeing a basket, aiming straight at it, using flash as light source and pressing the button is a good start. But then, one should think like "ok I have the shot, how can I improve it?" Try getting rid of direct light, change the field (and maybe depth) of view, postprocess your shot to emphasize the speciality of the selected pattern, do anything to grab the attention of the viewer. Oh, and the common word: it''s small. You have the size limit of an old monitor and the filesize limit not much less than the total memory of an old video card, so use it.</td>', 'Simplicity is great sometimes. Seeing a basket, aiming straight at it, using flash as light source and pressing the button is a good start. But then, one should think like "ok I have the shot, how can I improve it?" Try getting rid of direct light, change the field (and maybe depth) of view, postprocess your shot to emphasize the speciality of the selected pattern, do anything to grab the attention of the viewer. Oh, and the common word: it''s small. You have the size limit of an old monitor and the filesize limit not much less than the total memory of an old video card, so use it.', '2005-12-29 10:05:18.000000', NULL, 1),
