(2017492, 273158, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Definitely a creative idea. Technically it appears the exposure and color balance are right on. The colors go well together. Good composition also.<br/>Not much else to say really - a well executed shot.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** Definitely a creative idea. Technically it appears the exposure and color balance are right on. The colors go well together. Good composition also.Not much else to say really - a well executed shot. - Linda', '2006-01-09 05:19:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2017498, 272089, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>What a stunning capture! I love the clarity of the birds flying over head, especially with just the one showing it''s colors. Great focus! Colors are also very sharp - vivid. Truly impressive. Composesd perfectly also, almost as if you had placed the birds in the sky yourself. Great shooting!<br/>As for meeting the challenge, it was a bit of a stretch. I am guessing by the title your pattern was the pink pattern of the one bird?<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** What a stunning capture! I love the clarity of the birds flying over head, especially with just the one showing it''s colors. Great focus! Colors are also very sharp - vivid. Truly impressive. Composesd perfectly also, almost as if you had placed the birds in the sky yourself. Great shooting!As for meeting the challenge, it was a bit of a stretch. I am guessing by the title your pattern was the pink pattern of the one bird? - Linda', '2006-01-09 05:29:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2017506, 272973, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>The texture and pattern present in the leaves is nice, but the lighting is too harsh. As for the composition, I would have liked to see more angle to this instead of so straight down. Another idea would have been to use a shallow DOF, focusing on just one of the larger leaves. Just seems a little too busy to me. The colors are nice and vibrant where there is not glare, and very natural looking.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** The texture and pattern present in the leaves is nice, but the lighting is too harsh. As for the composition, I would have liked to see more angle to this instead of so straight down. Another idea would have been to use a shallow DOF, focusing on just one of the larger leaves. Just seems a little too busy to me. The colors are nice and vibrant where there is not glare, and very natural looking. - Linda', '2006-01-09 05:35:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2017523, 272742, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>B/W was an excellent choice for this image. Focus was real good, keeping the pattern of the nets crisp and clear. The lighting was not too harsh or too light - good job. The composition is also very well executed. You''ve got a good eye matey.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** B/W was an excellent choice for this image. Focus was real good, keeping the pattern of the nets crisp and clear. The lighting was not too harsh or too light - good job. The composition is also very well executed. You''ve got a good eye matey. - Linda', '2006-01-09 05:45:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2017558, 272889, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>I find this to be an interesting shot - great perspective. The light coming through is a bit harsh and would have been improved by adjusting your exposure factors. A real shame as it looks like there would have been a lot more detail. The composition is okay, although for shots like this a little bit of an angle that elongates is my preference - but not necessarily what you were after. I do think the off-centering was a good choice. Good leading lines here. Keep up the cfreative thinking and good luck with your future entries.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** I find this to be an interesting shot - great perspective. The light coming through is a bit harsh and would have been improved by adjusting your exposure factors. A real shame as it looks like there would have been a lot more detail. The composition is okay, although for shots like this a little bit of an angle that elongates is my preference - but not necessarily what you were after. I do think the off-centering was a good choice. Good leading lines here. Keep up the cfreative thinking and good luck with your future entries. - Linda', '2006-01-09 06:14:43.000000', NULL, 0),
